\ Scope enforcement: the barrier stops a scope reaching past its inputs.
\
\ The driver feeds the whole file to one ff_eval and ignores vtracef, so
\ a hard error ends the run and everything after it is skipped. The
\ expected output is therefore just the sentinel printed before the
\ violation — which is the assertion: the violation was caught, rather
\ than silently eating the caller's cells and carrying on.

\ `a b +` leaves one cell above the barrier; dropping twice asks for a
\ second. Without the barrier that drop would consume the caller's 111
\ and the damage would surface somewhere unrelated. (The compiler folds
\ `drop drop` into 2DROP, so the underflow is reported as needing two.)
: eat { ( a b -- c ) a b + drop drop } ;

\ Sentinel: everything up to the violation still runs.
7 .

111 222 1 2 eat

\ Never reached.
99 .
